- AXIS: TIMESCALE CONTRAST — the difference between the 10-day and 60-day rolling standard deviation of returns, scaled by the 30-day moving average of volume.
- AXIS: RESIDUAL — the residual from regressing daily return against the 60-day moving average of close prices, then ranked across stocks.
- AXIS: UNUSUAL PAIRING — the correlation between the daily range ($high - $low) and the daily return, calculated over a 30-day window.
- AXIS: SHAPE, NOT LEVEL — the skewness of the distribution of daily returns over a 60-day window, normalized by the median of the same period.
- AXIS: INVERSION — one minus the rank of the 30-day moving average of close prices, divided by the 60-day moving average of volume.
- AXIS: CROSS-FAMILY PRODUCT — the product of the 10-day RSI and the 30-day EMA of the close price, scaled by the 60-day SMA of volume.
- AXIS: DEPTH — the difference between the 10-day and 30-day rolling median of returns, divided by the 60-day rolling MAD of returns.
- AXIS: NEGLECTED OPERATOR — the DECAYLINEAR of the daily return over a 30-day window, divided by the 60-day moving average of volume.
- AXIS: ASYMMETRY — the conditional sum of positive daily returns over a 60-day window, divided by the total volume during that period.

