agent_trace.text:
- Short-term reversal driven by intraday range spikes in high-low prices precedes underperformance in next-day returns.
- Long-term reversal driven by cumulative intraday range expansions over 10-30 days precedes outperformance in next-month returns.
- Intraday range spikes in low prices, not high prices, precede underperformance in next-day returns.

RECIPES
- AXIS: ORDER STATISTICS — the position of the highest high within a 5-day window, divided by the number of trading days in the window. Uses $high, window=5.
- AXIS: UNUSUAL PAIRING — the correlation between daily volume and the range of the previous day's high-low, scaled by the standard deviation of the range. Uses $volume, $high, $low, window=20.
- AXIS: TIMESCALE CONTRAST — the difference between the 5-day moving average of the range and the 20-day moving average of the range, normalized by the 60-day standard deviation of the range. Uses $high, $low, window=5,20,60.
- AXIS: ODD NORMALISATION — the rank of the range relative to the median range across all stocks, divided by the rank of the return relative to the median return. Uses $high, $low, $return, window=10.
- AXIS: RESIDUAL — the residual of regressing daily returns on the squared range, then taking the negative of that residual. Uses $return, $high, $low, window=30.
- AXIS: ASYMMETRY — the difference between the 5-day moving average of the range when returns are positive versus when returns are negative. Uses $high, $low, $return, window=5.
- AXIS: CROSS-FAMILY PRODUCT — the product of the 20-day rolling skew of returns and the 20-day rolling kurtosis of volume. Uses $return, $volume, window=20.
- AXIS: INVERSION — one minus the ratio of the 10-day range to the 30-day range, scaled by the 60-day standard deviation of the range. Uses $high, $low, window=10,30,60.
- AXIS: SHAPE, NOT LEVEL — the difference between the 90th and 10th percentile of the range over a 60-day window, divided by the median range over the same period. Uses $high, $low, window=60.
- AXIS: NEGLECTED OPERATOR — the decay linear of the range over 20 days, multiplied by the inverse of the volume over the same period. Uses $high, $low, $volume, window=20.

